  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Monday)\nIssued at 308 AM CDT Tue Sep 15 2026\n\nThe center of the ridge is prog'd to slow/stall in the vicinity of ArkLaTex\nby Friday as a strong trough departs the Pacific northwest for the northern\nplains. This upper trough pushes a cold front southward across the plains\nand is forecast to arrive into at least northern Oklahoma by Saturday\nevening. Showers and thunderstorms chances have trended higher for late\nSaturday into Sunday morning, with beneficial and widespread rainfall\npossible. With moderate instability ahead of the front, strong to severe\nstorms are possible Saturday afternoon and evening. The latest NBM\nrun has high temperatures in the low 80's on Sunday and upper 70's\non Monday for areas near and north of the I-40 corridor. Southeastern\nOklahoma will be the last to benefit from the cooler airmass and is\nforecast to have max temperatures finally below 90 degrees on Monday.\nRain chances linger on Sunday and depart our area by Monday morning.\n\nThompson",
